The '''Strait of Ivorra''' ({{lang-bl|Estero de Ivorra}}), colloquially known as the '''Ivorran Passage''' is a body of water about 243 km (131 nmi; 151 mi) long, and 95 km (51 nmi; 59 mi) wide. The historical maritime border between [[Araucaria]] and [[Cerdanya]] runs down the centre of the Strait.{{Balisca articles}}
